    "summary": "Aman Kumar Sharma, an Indian mariner, describes his ordeal as a hostage of Somali pirates after his ship was seized in 2010, including mistreatment and a daring escape.",
    "content": "Aman Kumar Sharma, a seafarer from India, has publicly recounted his experience of being held captive by Somali pirates for 43 months. His vessel was hijacked in 2010, and he spent nearly four years in captivity before returning to India on 9 June 2014. Sharma's account provides a rare personal perspective on the hardships faced by crew members caught in pirate attacks off the Somali coast.\n\nAccording to Sharma, he endured physical abuse and was held for six months in forested areas of Somalia. The pirates also ran his ship aground before he eventually managed to escape through a planned breakout. He returned to India after almost four years in harsh conditions, including kidnapping and mistreatment.\n\nSharma's case is one of many involving foreign sailors taken hostage by Somali pirates during the peak of piracy in the late 2000s and early 2010s. At that time, attacks on commercial vessels were frequent, and crews were often held for extended periods while negotiations took place. The incident highlights the risks faced by international shipping in the region.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, Sharma's story serves as a reminder of the security challenges that have affected Somalia's image abroad. Many diaspora members have relatives who rely on maritime trade or have been indirectly affected by piracy. The case also underscores the importance of international efforts to combat piracy and ensure the safety of seafarers.\n\nSharma's return to India after years of captivity brings attention to the long-term psychological and physical toll on hostages. While piracy off Somalia has declined in recent years, the legacy of such incidents continues to shape perceptions and security measures in the region.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/18/badmaax-hindi-ah-oo-afar-sano-afduub-loogu-haystay-soomaaliya-oo-ka-sheekeeyay-dhibaatadii-uu-la-kulmay/",
